Now, each rose was sold for 4 dollars. To find out how much money she earned, I need to multiply the number of roses sold by the price per rose. So, 9 roses times 4 dollars per rose. Let me do that calculation: 9 times 4. Well, 9 times 4 is 36. So, that would mean she earned 36 dollars.

