41 - 29 = 12 \text{ seeds}
$$

These remaining 12 seeds were distributed equally into her small gardens, with **4 seeds per small garden**. To find the number of small gardens, divide the remaining seeds by the number of seeds per garden:

$$
12 \div 4 = 3
$$

Thus, Emily has $\boxed{3}$ small gardens. 

