Now, he wants to buy candy that costs 6 tickets each. So, how many candies can he buy? That means I need to divide the total tickets by the cost per candy. So 42 divided by 6. Let me calculate that. 6 times 7 is 42, right? So 42 divided by 6 is 7. 

