Apdil's dksfount flowers had a sale where each rose was sold for 7 dollars. April began with 9 roses and ended up with 4 roses left. To determine how much money she earned, we first calculate the number of roses she sold.

$$
\text{Roses sold} = \text{Beginning roses} - \text{Roses left} = 9 - 4 = 5
$$

Next, we calculate the total money earned from selling 5 roses at 7 dollars each:

$$
\text{Money earned} = \text{Roses sold} \times \text{Price per rose} = 5 \times 7 = 35
$$

Thus, the total amount of money April earned is:

$$
\boxed{35}
$$

