Okay, let's see. The cafeteria started with 96 apples. They gave out 42 to the students. Then they decided to use the rest to make pies. Each pie takes 6 apples. So, first, I need to figure out how many apples they have left after giving out 42.

So, subtract 42 from 96. Let me do that calculation: 96 minus 42. Hmm, 96 minus 40 is 56, and then minus 2 more is 54. So they have 54 apples left.

Now, they want to make pies with these 54 apples. Each pie requires 6 apples. So to find out how many pies they can make, I need to divide the number of apples by the number of apples per pie. That would be 54 divided by 6. Let me calculate that. 6 times 9 is 54, so 54 divided by 6 is 9. So they can make 9 pies.

Wait, let me check again. If they had 96 apples and gave away 42, 96-42 is indeed 54. Then 54 divided by 6 is 9. Yep, that seems right. I don't think I made any mistakes here. So the answer should be 9.

