Now, the problem says he wants to split these remaining 27 pieces into 9 equal loads. So, I need to divide 27 by 9 to find out how many clothes go into each small load. Let me do that division. 27 divided by 9 is 3. Wait, because 9 times 3 is 27. Yeah, that seems right. So each of the small loads would have 3 pieces of clothing.

