59 - 32 = 27
$$

Next, he splits the remaining 27 pieces into 9 equal loads. To determine how many pieces go into each load, we divide 27 by 9:

$$
27 \div 9 = 3
$$

Thus, each of the small loads contains 3 pieces of clothing. The calculations are correct and the result is a whole number, confirming no fractional pieces are involved.

$$
