Isabel had 2 pages of math homework and 4 pages of reading homework. Each page had 5 problems. 

First, we calculate the number of math problems:
$$ 2 \text{ pages} \times 5 \text{ problems per page} = 10 \text{ problems} $$

Next, we calculate the number of reading problems:
$$ 4 \text{ pages} \times 5 \text{ problems per page} = 20 \text{ problems} $$

Adding both together gives the total number of problems:
$$ 10 + 20 = 30 $$

The total number of problems Isabel had to complete is $\boxed{30}$. 

