The problem requires calculating the total earnings of Will over two days based on his hourly wage and the hours worked each day.

**Step 1: Calculate earnings on Monday**  
Will worked 8 hours on Monday at a rate of $8 per hour:  
$$
8 \, \text{hours} \times 8 \, \text{dollars/hour} = 64 \, \text{dollars}
$$  

**Step 2: Calculate earnings on Tuesday**  
Will worked 2 hours on Tuesday at the same rate:  
$$
2 \, \text{hours} \times 8 \, \text{dollars/hour} = 16 \, \text{dollars}
$$  

**Step 3: Add the earnings from both days**  
$$
64 \, \text{dollars} + 16 \, \text{dollars} = 80 \, \text{dollars}
$$  

Alternatively, we could calculate the total hours first and then multiply by the hourly rate:  
$$
(8 \, \text{hours} + 2 \, \text{hours}) \times 8 \, \text{dollars/hour} = 10 \, \text{hours} \times 8 \, \text{dollars/hour} = 80 \, \text{dollars}
$$  

